        "original_id": "53bbd5d0-3468-5b58-9289-4307aa578d8c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Cox Point, Garfield Glacier, Hull Bay, Marie Byrd Land\n- Organizations: United States Antarctic Service\n- People: Richard E. Byrd\n- Roles: Rear Admiral, American naval officer, explorer\n\nFacts:\n- Richard E. Byrd was born on October 25, 1888, and became an American naval officer who specialized in feats of exploration.\n- Cox Point was first observed and photographed from aircraft of the United States Antarctic Service during 1939–1941.\n- The United States Antarctic Service expedition of 1939–1941 was led by Admiral Richard E. Byrd.\n- Cox Point is a rock headland at the southwest side of the terminus of Garfield Glacier.\n- Garfield Glacier discharges into Hull Bay on the coast of Marie Byrd Land.\n- Richard E. Byrd died on March 11, 1957.",
